
# Default Properties in React

Default properties are default values assigned to component props.

If parent component does not pass value,
React uses default value automatically.

# Why Use Default Props?

Default props help:
- Avoid undefined values
- Provide fallback values
- Make components safer

# Example Without Default Props

## File Name: App.js

function Student(props){

    return(

        <h1>Hello {props.name}</h1>

    );

}

export default Student;